# THE ORACLE, CLOSED - Phase 54A checked by Phase 54B. Three steps over ONE
# corpus, and steps 1 and 2 never meet until step 3: the INTERPRETER runs the
# corpus with a recorder installed and writes what every register actually
# held; the COMPILER imports the same corpus, runs the inference, and writes
# what it claims every register will hold; tools/check/type-oracle.py compares
# the two. ZERO SOUNDNESS VIOLATIONS IS THE GATE; precision is reported, never
# gated ("soundness failing is a defect; precision being low is a backlog").
# The vacuous pass is guarded: `observed` must be positive, and so must
# `beat-boxed` - an inference that fell back to `boxed` everywhere is sound the
# way a stopped clock is right. A VALUE IN A LIVE BLOCK THE SOLVER NEVER
# VISITED is an analysis gap the emitter hides behind `boxed`, so its count is
# asserted at zero. The oracle's own self-test runs first.
#
# RUN: ctcompile-test-type-oracle
# RUN: ctcompile-test-type-oracle --script %S/claims.js --out %t.rec
# RUN: ctcompile-test-type-claims --script %S/claims.js --out %t.claims 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLAIMS
# CLAIMS: {{[^0-9]}}0 unvisited live values boxed
# RUN: python3 %{monorepo}/tools/check/type-oracle.py --recording %t.rec --claims %t.claims --name fixture --max-report 0 --expect-violations 0 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: observed registers {{ +[1-9][0-9]*}}
# CHECK: SOUNDNESS violations 0{{[^0-9]}}
# CHECK: PRECISION beat-boxed {{[1-9][0-9]*}}/{{[0-9]+}} = {{[0-9.]+}}%
